==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*toores}}, of {{etyl|bat|fi}} origin (compare Lithuanian {{term|dõras||good|lang=lt}}), with the suffix {{term|-e|lang=fi}}. The same reshaping has been applied in Karelian {{term|tuoreh|lang=krl}} and Votic {{term|toorõh|lang=vot}}. Estonian {{term|toores|lang=et}} retains the original stem type.

[[Category:Finnish words suffixed with -e]]

